hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2770","###\n Narrated to us Ali bin Mundhir, who narrated to us Ibn Fudail, who narrated to us Ata' bin Al-Sa'ib, from Kathir bin Jumhan Al-Sulami, who said: I saw Ibn Umar (RA) walking in the Sa'i (the area between Safa and Marwah). I said to him, \Are you walking in the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah?\"" He replied"","" \""If I am running"","" I have indeed seen the Prophet (ﷺ) running; and if I am"""""
"2771","Narrated to us Abu Musa, narrated to us Ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad, from Sufyan, from 'Ata ibn As-Sa'ib, from Kathir ibn Jumhan who said: \I saw Ibn 'Umar walking between As-Safa and Al-Marwah. So I said to him: 'Should I walk?' He replied: 'If you walk"","" then I have seen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) walking"","" and if you run"","" then I have seen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) running.'\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"2772","Narrated to us Abu Musa, then in succession, narrated to us al-Dahhak, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar (RA), a similar narration.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"2773","Narrated to us Saʿīd ibn Bashīr: Qatādah narrated to me, on the authority of ʿIkrimah, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) performed the *saʿy* (ritual walk between Ṣafā and Marwah) one year running and another year walking at a normal pace.\n\nIt was narrated by Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā: al-Mughīrah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Bashīr narrated to us.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
